the target language is: prolog.

the templates are:
    the calculation date is *a date*; scenario element.
    *a person* is a member of *a household*; scenario element.
    the snap household of *a household* has elderly or disabled member.
    the snap member of *a person* is elderly or disabled; scenario element.

the knowledge base us_statutes_7_2012_j includes:


% 7 U.S.C. 2012(j) — us:statutes/7/2012/j
the text of "7 USC 2012(j)" is at "sources/us/statutes/7/2012/j.yaml".

rule snap_household_has_elderly_or_disabled_member with provenance "7 USC 2012(j)":
the snap household of a household has elderly or disabled member if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2008-10-01 <= D
    and the household is a household
    and a number N is the count of each P such that
        a person P is a member of the household
    and a number K is the count of each M such that
        a person M is a member of the household
        and it is not the case that the snap member of M is elderly or disabled
    and N - K > 0.

scenario household_has_elderly_or_disabled_member is, as stated in "sources/us/statutes/7/2012/j.test.yaml" at case 1:
    household_1 is a household.
    the calculation date is 2026-01-01.
    person_1 is a person.
    person_1 is a member of household_1.
    the snap member of person_1 is elderly or disabled.
    q_snap_household_has_elderly_or_disabled_member expects answers ["the snap household of household_1 has elderly or disabled member"].

scenario household_without_elderly_or_disabled_member is, as stated in "sources/us/statutes/7/2012/j.test.yaml" at case 2:
    household_1 is a household.
    the calculation date is 2026-01-01.
    q_snap_household_has_elderly_or_disabled_member expects answers [].

query q_snap_household_has_elderly_or_disabled_member is:
    the snap household of which household has elderly or disabled member.

query q_snap_household_has_elderly_or_disabled_member is:
    the snap household of which household has elderly or disabled member.

